local MCP declares requiresBinary but the binary isn't found (the run(`which
${mcp.requiresBinary}`) branch), explicitly disable any existing registration
instead of merely continuing: set config.tools[mcp.toolPattern] = false (as
already done) and also clear or disable the MCP entry in the app config/registry
where MCPs are stored (e.g., the map/list keyed by mcp.name or mcp.id) so a
previously-registered MCP cannot stay enabled; keep the continue to skip
registration after disabling. Ensure you update the same config object used for
